        },
        {
          "text": "The triad built on the [[tonic|tonic]] is the [[tonic-triad|tonic triad]]. It is the chord that sounds like home. In C major it is C, E and G, with the tonic at the bottom.",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "keyboard",
            "highlight": [
              "C4",
              "E4",
              "G4"
            ],
            "low": "C4",
            "high": "C5"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Every key has one. G major: G, B, D. D major: D, F♯, A. F major: F, A, C. In D major the F♯ comes from the [[key-signature|key signature]], so no sharp is written beside it.",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "passage",
